  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Open {{appUrl}} and sign in through Cloudflare Access. An email listed under Administrators can open {{appUrl}}/admin to set the site's name, logo and the models everyone gets."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Agents need a model before the first chat: each user adds one with their own provider key in the app's settings, or set the AI Gateway fields in this app's settings to give everyone the gateway's models."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "To let people connect an outside service, create an OAuth app with that service and enter its client ID and secret in this app's settings. Each service sends people back to its own address: {{appUrl}}/gatekeeper/github/oauth for GitHub, and the same with google, slack, notion, linear, cloudflare, confluence, spotify, supabase or zoominfo in place of github. Home Assistant and MCP servers need no client: people connect them in the app. Adding or removing a custom domain moves these addresses to the new domain, so register the new callback address with every OAuth client then."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Every Appflare user can sign in."
    }
  ],
  // Upstream moves several times a day and its deploy contract
  // (scripts/release/manifest-lib.ts) changes with it, so a maintainer
  // reads each bump before it publishes.
  "bump": { "autoMerge": false }
}
